          "content": "HOVER CARD ANCHORING",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BRyLN",
          "name": "rule 1",
          "fill": "#727272",
          "content": "bars 1 to 4 · card flush left with the bar",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "OGXIM",
          "name": "rule 2",
          "fill": "#727272",
          "content": "bars 5 to 10 · card centred on the bar",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "vGxFO",
          "name": "rule 3",
          "fill": "#727272",
          "content": "bars 11 to 14 · card flush right with the bar",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JUMs3",
          "name": "rule note",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The card is anchored by bar index, so it always lands inside the panel. Four bars at each end and not two: the card is 190 wide and a bar is a fourteenth of the panel, so at the narrowest two column width centring the third one already hangs it off the edge. Nothing overflows to the right, and the Usage page never scrolls sideways.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "VpWw6",
      "x": 13024,
      "y": 1240,
      "name": "Chat · replies that came back empty",
      "width": 900,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "stroke": "$border",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ft2WL",
          "name": "h",
          "fill": "#727272",
          "content": "CHAT · REPLIES THAT CAME BACK EMPTY",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xnmHu",
          "name": "rule cap",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A run of replies where Hermes wrote out its own format example instead of an answer. Nothing is deleted: they stay in the conversation on disk, and the flag that spots them is worked out at read time. But a bubble that says nothing must not read as a message, so a run folds into one line that says how many there were, in the place they happened, and opens on demand.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11.5,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rRepx",
